nsumer segments. The company offers wheels, tires, and components for various agricultural equipment, including tractors, combines, skidders, plows, planters, and irrigation equipment; and agricultural tires under the Goodyear Farm Tire, Titan Tire, Carlstar, ACES, and Voltyre-Prom brands. It also provides wheels, tires, and undercarriage systems and components for various types of off-the-road earthmoving, mining, military, construction, and forestry equipment, such as skid steers, aerial lifts, cranes, graders and levelers, scrapers, self-propelled shovel loaders, articulated dump trucks, load transporters, haul trucks, backhoe loaders, crawler tractors, lattice cranes, shovels, and hydraulic excavators under the Titan brand. In addition, the company manufactures and distributes wheels and tires for end-market verticals comprising outdoor power equipment, power sports, and high speed trailers; and manufactures and sells small to midsize agricultural tires under the Carlstar, ITP, Black Rock, Goodyear, and Unique brands. Further, it is involved in the provision of wheel and tire assembly services; manufactures bias truck and light truck tires; and sale of rubber stocks. The company sells its products directly to original equipment manufacturers, as well as to the aftermarket through independent distributors, equipment dealers, and its distribution centers. Titan International, Inc. was founded in 1890 and is headquartered in West Chicago, Illinois.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Paul George Reitz | CEO, President & Director | Age 53 | Compensation: $1.7M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 8K people. Revenue per employee of $223K ranks in the bottom quartile among Industrials peers. Stock-based compensation of $400 per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 8\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Titan International, Inc. (DE) is a small-cap industrials business with a $319M market cap on $1.8B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -6% over the past three years and +3% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 14% against a 7% cost of capital, a 7-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it, and 13% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The company is burning through $25M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 4.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 0.5\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 5.8% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.1\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.8) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Heavy insider selling (net $27.2M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-27219527.6},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Industrials peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Industrials peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Industrials peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Industrials peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 13% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 26% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Noble Financial Analysts Decrease Earnings Estimates for TWI","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/04/noble-financial-analysts-decrease-earnings-estimates-for-twi.html","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793796199.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.94,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"What Titan International (TWI) Said on Its Q3 Earnings Call","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/02/what-titan-international-twi-said-on-its-q3-earnings-call.html","date":"2026-11-02","timestamp":1793599988.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.368,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Titan (TWI) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/titan-twi-q3-2026-earnings-170058000.html","date":"2026-10-31","timestamp":1793466562.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.527,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Titan International (NYSE:TWI) Stock Rating Cut to \u201cSell\u201d at Wall Street Zen","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/10/31/titan-internation